% Plummer cluster with a REALISTIC binary population (Type 5 stars).
% Units: pc - km/s - Msun, so G = 4.302e-3 in code units.
% 256 systems -> ~335 stars, ~130 Msun; Kroupa IMF, Duchene & Kraus binary fraction,
% Raghavan period distribution, thermal eccentricities. See make_..._ics.py.
%
% RUNTIME IS SET BY THE TIGHTEST PERICENTRE, not by the number of stars: that pair's
% orbit fixes the smallest timestep and therefore the global sync cadence. Measured
% scaling at M=1 Msun, dt ~ t_dyn(peri)/30:
%     peri 1000 AU -> 3.0e4 steps      peri 100 AU -> 9.5e5 steps
%      peri 300 AU -> 1.8e5 steps       peri  20 AU -> 1.1e7 steps
% per unit TimeMax=32.4. The equal-mass test sits at the top of that table (1000 AU,
% circular) and costs 15-40 min. This test keeps a 100 AU pericentre floor -- which
% preserves a ~50x spread in binary hardness, and with the a-range gives ~8 timebins
% of spread, the diversity the test exists for -- and pays for it by running 10x
% shorter: TimeMax 3.24 rather than 32.4. Net cost lands within a few x of the
% equal-mass test.
%
% 3.24 code time is ~1 half-mass crossing, so this measures CONSERVATION under a
% realistic population, not cluster relaxation. Lagrange-radius evolution needs the
% longer run; do not read structural evolution off this one.
%
% RUNTIME IS UNMEASURED as of writing -- the estimate above is analytic. Calibrate on
% a compute node before treating the cost as known.
%
InitCondFile                       plummer_binaries_realistic_ics
OutputDir                          output
TimeMax                            29.2
BoxSize                            300
TimeBetSnapshot                    0.292
TimeOfFirstSnapshot                0
TimeBegin                          0
TimeBetStatistics                  0.3
MaxSizeTimestep                    0.05
MinSizeTimestep                    1e-12
ErrTolIntAccuracy                  0.005
ErrTolTheta                        0.5
ErrTolForceAcc                     0.0025
CourantFac                         0.4
MaxRMSDisplacementFac              0.125
TreeDomainUpdateFrequency          0.1
DesNumNgb                          32
MaxNumNgbDeviation                 1
MaxMemSize                         2000
PartAllocFactor                    2.5
BufferSize                         100
ResubmitOn                         0
ResubmitCommand                    none
UnitLength_in_cm                   3.085678e+18
UnitMass_in_g                      1.989e+33
UnitVelocity_in_cm_per_s           100000
Softening_Type0                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type1                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type2                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type3                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type4                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type5                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type0_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type1_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type2_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type3_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type4_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type5_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
AGS_DesNumNgb                      32
AGS_MaxNumNgbDeviation             1
CritPhysDensity                    1e13
CpuTimeBetRestartFile              30
% Cap sink accretion-search at the softening kernel radius (18 AU = 8.726e-5 pc).
% With no gas in this test the default 5 pc search radius wastes huge amounts of
% tree-walking; shrinking it to the softening scale eliminates that overhead.
SinkMaxAccretionRadius             8.726e-5
